<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i)));</code>

However, since the comment specifies that the list should be equal to the collection after all its elements have been added, we need to ensure that the size of the list matches the size of the collection and that all elements match. The correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
